"QUERYGRID:"
"a0.lot","lot","Y","None","None","Row","c","Identifies a batch of wafers or units being processed in the factory.The basic format of the Lot number is:  FYWWNNNN where F=fab code, Y=year, WW=workweek, NNNN= sequence, with the 9th or 10th characters as alphanumeric. In Fab, Etest and Sort, a quantity that has a wafer as an unit of measure and the physical form that passes through the factory. A lot starting the Fab process contains up to 25 wafers and can be split into child lots of varying sizes, and wafer losses can also occur. New lots are also created to split lots due to varying characteristics, such as speed or rework, for a portion of the lot. In some 200mm fabs production lots, the lot number uses a silicon vendor ID in the 8th character","f_lothist","a0->f0.lot","col1"
"a0.create_data1","create_data1","Y","None","None","Row","c","Stores optional data entered by the user when a lot is created.","f_lot","a0->f9.create_data1","col33"
"a0.create_data2","create_data2","Y","None","None","Row","c","Stores the NT userid that owns the lot.  e.g., AMR\johndoe","f_lot","a0->f9.create_data2","col34"
"a0.create_data3","create_data3","Y","None","None","Row","c","Stores Copper (CU)  Contaminant information related to the lot . Used to identify materials that would contaminate the lot if cross-processing occurs on a piece of equipment.  This is a flag with valid values of 'Y' or 'N'.  The previous values listed in the mapping apply only to operation contaminants, not lot contaminants (no subcategories here).  A lot may contain more than one contaminant at the same time (Cu and Pb are common).  Contaminants are listed in MARS under create_data3 (Cu), create_data6 (Pb), and create_data7 (Au).","f_lot","a0->f9.create_data3","col35"
"a0.create_data4","create_data4","Y","None","None","Row","c","Stores optional data entered by the user when a lot is created.","f_lot","a0->f9.create_data4","col36"
"a0.inqty","inqty","Y","None","None","Row","n","The quantity of units or wafers in the lot when it arrived at the operation.","f_lothist","a0->f0.inqty","col39"
